#
#  is not optional: it is what produced the committed file
# (see its header). Kept in step with  in
#  by a test in that script's suite.
mkdocs>=1.6.1,<2
# Material for MkDocs reaches EOL on 2026-11-05 (Issue #3990).
# Decision matrix (documented in docs/reference/mkdocs-material-coupling.md):
# 1. GHSA security advisory against mkdocs-material -> immediate theme migration.
# 2. Build-chain incompatibility on required Python/mkdocs version -> forced migration.
# 3. Calendar check at v3.19.0 milestone (2026-10-08) -> re-evaluate status.
# No  extra: the  plugin it fed made every docs build
# fetch Inter/JetBrains Mono from fonts.google.com at build time (see
# mkdocs.yml history and docs/reference/mkdocs-material-coupling.md). That
# fetch is what broke the Read the Docs build - a network dependency inside
# a build step for a project whose stated goal is air-gap friendliness.
# Dropped rather than made resilient: nothing else in this repo needs it.

